<Layout title="Programmer’s Reference Manual" description="A reference for pTOS development covering system interfaces, calling conventions and compatibility.">
  <header class="directory-head">
    <h1>pTOS Programmer’s<br />Reference Manual</h1>
  </header>
  <p>This manual is a reference for pTOS development. It documents operating system calls, GEM interfaces,
    executable formats and calling conventions for 68k, ARM and x32. It covers pTOS extensions and build
    requirements, compatibility with TOS and ParaTOS, and GFA BASIC bindings.</p>
  <p>Many pTOS extensions build on interfaces from FreeMiNT and MagiC. pTOS aims for compatibility with those
    systems where practical. The reference describes differences in supported calls, modes and behavior.</p>
  <p>The manual draws on external references that the pTOS team has edited and extended for this site.
    The pTOS team is responsible for any errors or omissions here. See <a href="/sources/">Sources and licensing</a>
    for attribution, revisions and license details.</p>
</Layout>
